#basePath Day0

::OpeningPrelude
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@who    Astrid

$call InitUpdateMasks()
{@Astrid} Come on, Elijah, where are you? It’s already starting! $[Prelude/Astrid/01]
 
$call Wait(1)
(*phone buzzing sfx*)
 
{@Elijah} Astrid, I’m so sorry I’m late! There was something going on at the lab, some weird anomaly— $[Prelude/Elijah/01]

{@Astrid} Ooh, that sounds mysterious.
Did they discover a new comet or something?
 
{@Elijah} I don’t know. Told them I had a party to get to.
 
{@Astrid} Good. The Perseids aren’t gonna wait forever.
 
{@Elijah} Wow . . . it’s incredible.
 
{@Astrid} Yeah. It never gets old.
 
{@Elijah} Just think . . . next year on your birthday we’ll be astronomy majors in college, watching the meteor shower together. I hear UW has some great stargazing spots.
 
{@Astrid} My aunt doesn’t think we’ll be together next year. $[Prelude/Astrid/03]

{@Elijah} What? Why not? $[Prelude/Elijah/03]
 
{@Astrid} She says it won’t last. Things change. $[Prelude/Astrid/04]
 
{@Elijah} Of course things change. So what? We can still be together. $[Prelude/Elijah/04]
Trust me, Astrid. It’s written in the stars.
$call Wait(2)
Did you read my birthday card? $[Prelude/Elijah/06]

{@Elijah} “Set me as a seal upon your heart, as a seal upon your arm.”
$call Wait(1)
Sorry . . . too cheesy?

{@Astrid} Maybe a little. But I liked it. 
Who’s the drawing supposed to be? $[Prelude/Astrid/07]
 
{@Elijah} It’s you! I drew you as Perseus. $[Prelude/Elijah/07]
 
{@Astrid} Like . . . the constellation? $[Prelude/Astrid/08]
 
{@Elijah} Exactly. It’s based on a Greek myth.
This meteor shower is called the Perseids because Perseus is its radiant.
You know . . . the point in the sky where the meteor shower looks like it’s starting. $[Prelude/Elijah/09]
 
{@Astrid} Wow . . . I’ve watched the Perseids every year since I was six, and I never knew that. $[Prelude/Astrid/10]
I guess Dad and I were more focused on finding Ursa Major and Ursa Minor. I used to call them Papa Bear and Little Bear. 
Is Perseus visible from here? $[Prelude/Astrid/11]
 
{@Elijah} Sure. It’s easy to find. $[Prelude/Elijah/11]
Just look for the place where the meteors seem to be coming from.
If you move your phone across the sky, it’ll tell you if you’re getting warmer or colder.
 
 
{@Astrid} Found it! $[Prelude/Astrid/12]
We’re so lucky to have the sky all mapped out.
It would take forever to figure all this out from scratch.
 
{@Elijah} I don’t know. Sounds sort of fun to me.
 
{@Astrid} Hey, I never said it wouldn’t be fun. $[Prelude/Astrid/13]
Now you have to explain. How am I like Perseus?
Didn’t he get cast out to sea by his dad, and then end up becoming some big hero?
 
{@Elijah} Exactly! He went on a quest, fell in love with the princess Andromeda, and saved her from a sea monster. $[Prelude/Elijah/14]
 
{@Astrid} Stillll not seeing how that’s like me.
 
{@Elijah} Come on. Isn’t it obvious? Your dad’s off doing research at the South Pole, so you’ve been cast out to that little town with your aunt. $[Prelude/Elijah/15]
You’re about to start your senior year at a brand new school. And you’re still completely fearless. $[Prelude/Elijah/16]
 
{@Astrid} My aunt was right. You’re such a hopeless romantic. $[Prelude/Astrid/17]

{@Elijah} Romantic? Sure. But hopeless? Never.$[Prelude/Elijah/18]
 
{@Astrid} So if I’m Perseus, does that make you Andromeda? $[Prelude/Astrid/18]
 
{@Elijah} I don’t know. I think I’m more of a— $[Prelude/Elijah/19]
 
{@Astrid} Elijah? Hello? $[Prelude/Astrid/19]
$call Wait(2) 
Whoa. Elijah, are you seeing this? $[Prelude/Astrid/20]

{@Elijah} Astrid—you’re breaking up— $[Prelude/Elijah/20]
 
{@Astrid} Is that the Northern Lights? $[Prelude/Astrid/21]
Whoa. It’s so bright!
 
{@Elijah} (*bzzzzzzz krrrrrrr*) —Something’s not right— $[Prelude/Elijah/21]
(*static noises*) —Readings off the charts— (*brrrrrr kzzzzzz*)
 
{@Astrid} Elijah, can you hear me? $[Prelude/Astrid/22]
$call Wait(2) 
Hello? Elijah? $[Prelude/Astrid/23]

$call LoadNextDay()
